WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
Supernova nineteen eighty seven A occurred in the

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.900
Large Magellanic Cloud. Its short neutrino burst directly

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.720
supported the collapse energy channel. Only a tiny

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.780
sample was detected: most particles missed Earth, and

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.620
most crossing a detector passed through without interacting.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.400
Detected counts do not equal the total emitted.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:21.870
The circumstellar ring was already present before the

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.390
explosion. Ejecta and the outward shock traveled toward

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.350
it. When the shock encountered dense knots, energy

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:31.170
deposited in the gas caused brightening. The changing

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.010
ring therefore records an interaction with the progenitor’s

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.370
earlier surroundings, rather than newly formed ring material.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.610
A Sun like star sheds a planetary nebula

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:44.010
and leaves a white dwarf. Successful massive core

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.990
collapse can leave a neutron star; continued collapse

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:49.410
can lead to a black hole. Specify the

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:52.510
pathway before choosing a remnant. A missing central

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.570
detection, by itself, does not uniquely establish a

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:56.350
black hole.
